WEBVTT

00:01.021 --> 00:02.981
[♪ opening theme song playing]

01:37.951 --> 01:39.331
Hang on.
I know Kikuchi said

01:39.411 --> 01:40.791
figuring out
the joker's position

01:40.871 --> 01:43.411
would let him win,
but is that really the case?

01:43.501 --> 01:44.831
Seems kinda arbitrary.

01:44.921 --> 01:47.291
Like for this hand,
Akiyama cuts second,

01:47.381 --> 01:50.381
so the chances of drawing
the joker are even, right?

01:50.461 --> 01:53.011
That's right, more or less.

01:53.091 --> 01:55.301
At the very least,
he didn't draw the joker

01:55.381 --> 01:56.891
-from the start.
-I know!

01:56.971 --> 01:58.601
If the joker stays
in the deck,

01:58.681 --> 02:00.561
then Kikuchi's plan falls apart.

02:00.641 --> 02:03.231
No way he can guarantee
he'll get it at that point.

02:03.311 --> 02:05.151
How can that be a sure win?

02:05.231 --> 02:07.231
-There's more to it.
-Huh?

02:07.731 --> 02:11.111
To put it simply, if Kikuchi's
in position to draw first,

02:11.191 --> 02:13.611
then that means Akiyama
has exactly zero chance

02:13.701 --> 02:14.861
of ending up with the joker.

02:14.951 --> 02:16.031
What?

02:16.111 --> 02:17.911
Let's assume that for this hand,

02:17.991 --> 02:19.911
the joker ended up
on top of the deck.

02:19.991 --> 02:23.751
If Kikuchi discards first,
then he's guaranteed to get it.

02:23.831 --> 02:25.581
So in that case,
he has to just focus

02:25.671 --> 02:27.211
on bleeding Akiyama dry.

02:27.291 --> 02:29.421
But what about the other times?

02:29.501 --> 02:32.131
[DEALER] With that, we'll move
on to the discard phase.

02:32.211 --> 02:34.051
Mr. Kikuchi?

02:34.131 --> 02:37.431
Let's see. I think I'll discard
five this time.

02:37.511 --> 02:39.641
Why is he dumping
his entire hand?

02:39.721 --> 02:41.601
Because the joker
is the fifth card

02:41.681 --> 02:43.101
down in the deck.

02:44.981 --> 02:46.941
-[gasps]
-You see it now?

02:47.021 --> 02:49.771
As long as the joker's
somewhere in the top five cards,

02:49.861 --> 02:51.821
it may as well have been
in Kikuchi's hand

02:51.901 --> 02:52.901
from the beginning.

02:53.361 --> 02:55.321
That's all well and good
if it's high in the deck,

02:55.401 --> 02:57.321
but if it's six
or seven cards down,

02:57.411 --> 02:59.201
couldn't Akiyama
wind up with it?

02:59.281 --> 03:00.831
Not necessarily.

03:00.911 --> 03:01.871
In this game,

03:02.331 --> 03:03.951
you'll always have something
in your first hand,

03:04.041 --> 03:06.041
and the worst
it can be is a pair.

03:06.121 --> 03:08.001
So it's extremely unlikely

03:08.081 --> 03:10.881
that Akiyama will discard
more than three cards per hand.

03:10.961 --> 03:12.711
[NISHIDA] Oh, okay.

03:12.801 --> 03:14.591
With no reason
to expect Akiyama

03:14.671 --> 03:16.431
to ask for more than
three cards,

03:16.511 --> 03:18.551
all Kikuchi needs is one or two.

03:18.641 --> 03:21.351
That way, neither of them
ends up with the joker.

03:21.431 --> 03:24.101
So really, it doesn't matter
where the joker is.

03:24.181 --> 03:26.481
Akiyama's chances
of getting it are nil.

03:26.561 --> 03:29.101
Whereas Kikuchi's
are overwhelming.

03:29.191 --> 03:30.901
That's why he's going to win.

03:31.441 --> 03:35.111
Yeah, sure. But isn't scrapping
his whole hand still risky?

03:35.191 --> 03:37.901
Not in the slightest.
Akiyama made sure of that

03:37.991 --> 03:40.111
by taking two cards last draw.

03:40.201 --> 03:44.241
Because now all 17 cards
in the deck have been in play.

03:44.331 --> 03:46.291
-[NISHIDA] So?
-[KOSAKA] Out of those 17,

03:46.371 --> 03:48.501
ten have passed through
Kikuchi's hand.

03:48.581 --> 03:50.421
And through process
of elimination,

03:50.501 --> 03:52.081
he can deduce which cards

03:52.171 --> 03:54.381
-Akiyama was dealt this hand.
-[NISHIDA] Oh!

03:54.461 --> 03:56.011
And of those cards,

03:56.091 --> 03:57.761
the best hand
he could possibly make

03:57.841 --> 04:00.641
would be two pair,
which Kikuchi can defeat easily.

04:00.721 --> 04:01.641
[NISHIDA] Oh.

04:01.721 --> 04:03.301
[DEALER] Open!

04:07.851 --> 04:08.931
All right!

04:09.641 --> 04:11.231
[SOLARIO] With three of a kind,
Kikuchi wins the hand.

04:11.311 --> 04:13.191
And 20 chips
go to the Western Army.

04:14.361 --> 04:15.901
[Nao gasps]

04:16.941 --> 04:18.901
[DEALER] The fifth hand
will now begin.

04:25.661 --> 04:29.041
Look, he got the joker,
which makes four of a kind.

04:29.121 --> 04:31.751
[DEALER] The first bet
is yours, Mr. Kikuchi.

04:32.211 --> 04:34.461
[KIKUCHI] You know what?
I'm gonna fold.

04:34.541 --> 04:36.001
[Nao gasps]

04:36.091 --> 04:39.221
[SOLARIO] And with that,
the fifth hand is incomplete.

04:39.631 --> 04:41.891
The five-chip antes
go to the dealer,

04:41.971 --> 04:44.681
while the chip balance
remains unchanged.

04:44.761 --> 04:47.561
Really? We had
such a good hand, though.

04:47.641 --> 04:49.141
And why fold?

04:49.231 --> 04:51.811
All that did was remove chips
out of the game.

04:51.901 --> 04:53.191
What was that?

04:53.271 --> 04:55.821
Akiyama started out
with the joker in his hand.

04:55.901 --> 04:59.361
Folding right out of the gate
minimizes our losses.

04:59.441 --> 05:03.281
And furthermore, it sets him up
to cut second in the next hand.

05:03.371 --> 05:05.331
So now he can manipulate
the deck

05:05.411 --> 05:07.121
to get the joker
in his opening hand.

05:07.201 --> 05:08.581
Well, that's good.

05:13.961 --> 05:15.581
There it is.

05:15.671 --> 05:16.961
Incredible.

05:17.041 --> 05:19.461
[DEALER] That concludes
this round of betting.

05:19.551 --> 05:20.671
Now then...

05:20.761 --> 05:22.171
Open!

05:24.551 --> 05:25.721
Oh, yeah!

05:26.101 --> 05:27.971
[SOLARIO] The Western Army
wins with four of a kind.

05:28.561 --> 05:31.351
That's 20 chips directly
into their war chest,

05:31.431 --> 05:33.561
putting them in the lead by 18.

05:33.651 --> 05:35.061
[NAO] What?!

05:36.941 --> 05:39.151
[Kikuchi chuckles]

05:39.231 --> 05:41.571
The Core match
is as good as ours!

05:42.111 --> 05:43.321
-[AKIYAMA] I see you.
-Hmm?

05:44.031 --> 05:46.121
You're following the joker.

05:46.201 --> 05:48.701
What? Don't be ridiculous.

05:48.781 --> 05:51.581
What's ridiculous is
how obvious you are.

05:51.661 --> 05:54.041
A neon sign would be
more subtle.

05:54.121 --> 05:56.501
Drawing four cards
in the practice round.

05:56.581 --> 05:58.961
Discarding your whole hand
in the fourth.

05:59.041 --> 06:01.511
And then the first time
I start off with the Joker,

06:01.591 --> 06:02.721
you fold.

06:02.801 --> 06:04.971
There can be
only one clear explanation

06:05.051 --> 06:06.341
for your behavior.

06:06.431 --> 06:09.011
You know exactly
where the joker is at all times.

06:09.761 --> 06:11.311
That's stupid.

06:11.851 --> 06:13.101
And impossible.

06:13.181 --> 06:15.101
How can I know
where any one card is?

06:15.691 --> 06:17.481
We play with a new deck
each hand.

06:17.561 --> 06:19.691
I think you must be
imagining things.

06:19.771 --> 06:21.901
But then,
it's natural to get jumpy

06:21.981 --> 06:23.571
when you're on the back foot.

06:23.651 --> 06:25.321
[smirks] Jumpy.

06:25.401 --> 06:27.621
Yeah, sure,
that must be what it is.

06:27.701 --> 06:28.911
Timeout!

06:29.331 --> 06:31.161
[SOLARIO] The Eastern Army calls
a timeout for this hand.

06:31.241 --> 06:34.581
You have three minutes
to confer, starting now.

06:34.661 --> 06:36.421
Looks like you're not alone.

06:36.501 --> 06:38.461
Guess it must be
something in the air.

06:40.631 --> 06:42.261
[door slides open]

06:42.341 --> 06:44.841
So is this thing
in the bag or what?

06:44.921 --> 06:46.051
[KIKUCHI] Possibly.

06:46.131 --> 06:47.891
Akiyama's somehow figured out

06:47.971 --> 06:50.141
that I'm keeping track
of where the joker is.

06:50.221 --> 06:51.431
Should we be worried?

06:51.511 --> 06:54.061
Of course not.
Doesn't matter if he knows.

06:54.141 --> 06:55.981
There's nothing
he can do about it.

06:56.061 --> 06:58.941
Because I'm the only one
who can use my trick.

06:59.021 --> 07:00.571
-[NAO] Sorry to intrude.
-Mm?

07:02.191 --> 07:03.861
What is going on here?

07:04.401 --> 07:07.611
So, I want to propose a truce.

07:08.201 --> 07:09.371
-What?
-A truce?

07:10.491 --> 07:13.701
Please listen. I swear,
we want to save you.

07:13.791 --> 07:16.211
Whatever this is,
the answer's no.

07:16.291 --> 07:18.791
Wait, let's hear her out.
I'm curious.

07:18.881 --> 07:20.501
Let me explain.

07:20.581 --> 07:23.251
We chose to finish
the Spearhead match in a tie.

07:23.341 --> 07:25.261
Do you know why we did that?

07:25.341 --> 07:27.721
Because for us to win,
we would have had to pass,

07:27.801 --> 07:30.141
and that would have meant
sacrificing a lot of chips

07:30.221 --> 07:32.061
from both our pools
to the dealer.

07:32.141 --> 07:34.021
Which would shrink
the total pot...

07:34.101 --> 07:36.641
Hurting all of us
in the long run. Do you see?

07:36.731 --> 07:39.061
What are you talking about,
"total pot"?

07:39.151 --> 07:42.271
[NAO] The LGT office handed us
900 million in chips,

07:42.361 --> 07:44.651
but they said they'd
only be collecting six.

07:45.281 --> 07:48.401
That leaves 300 million
on the table for us to win.

07:49.151 --> 07:50.991
That money can save
multiple people,

07:51.071 --> 07:53.281
but we need to work together
to get all of it.

07:53.371 --> 07:56.161
If you agree to concede
this revival round to us,

07:56.251 --> 07:57.791
we swear we'll use that money

07:57.871 --> 07:59.671
to free you all
from the Liar Game!

07:59.751 --> 08:01.881
-[NISHIDA] Uh?
-What a load of bull.

08:01.961 --> 08:03.881
No, I think she means it.

08:03.961 --> 08:05.301
They did go for a draw

08:05.381 --> 08:07.131
in the Spearhead match
after all.

08:07.211 --> 08:08.471
You're buying this?

08:08.551 --> 08:10.051
I don't know why
they caused a draw,

08:10.141 --> 08:11.261
but I know this much...

08:11.341 --> 08:13.601
Self-sabotage
never saved anyone!

08:13.681 --> 08:14.851
But we can!

08:15.521 --> 08:18.021
Nao, stop.
You tried making your pitch,

08:18.101 --> 08:19.771
but they're not going for it.

08:20.481 --> 08:21.811
But still...

08:21.901 --> 08:24.571
[SOLARIO] Your brief
intermission is now over.

08:24.651 --> 08:26.781
Both players,
please return to the table.

08:33.821 --> 08:35.581
-[KIKUCHI] Question.
-Hmm?

08:35.661 --> 08:39.291
Was any of that Kanzaki girl's
babbling believable?

08:39.371 --> 08:41.921
Are you really attempting
to save all of us?

08:42.001 --> 08:43.001
[AKIYAMA] Yes.

08:44.041 --> 08:47.011
If I'm being honest,
that doesn't sound too bad.

08:47.091 --> 08:49.881
[gasps] You hear that?
We're one step closer

08:49.971 --> 08:52.641
to making a truce with them.
[chuckles]

08:52.721 --> 08:55.221
[DEALER]
Mr. Kikuchi, your first bet.

08:55.301 --> 08:58.731
[KIKUCHI] I think I'll go
with a maximum of 15 chips.

09:00.351 --> 09:02.941
[DEALER] Mr. Akiyama,
how will you respond?

09:03.021 --> 09:05.021
[KIKUCHI] Well, you're going
to call, right?

09:05.561 --> 09:07.571
You said you wanted to save us.

09:07.651 --> 09:10.401
Can't do that if the dealer
gets all those chips.

09:11.241 --> 09:12.451
Guess I'll call.

09:12.531 --> 09:14.031
[Kikuchi laughs]

09:14.121 --> 09:15.531
How considerate of you.

09:15.621 --> 09:17.121
-[Nao gasps]
-Well, isn't that

09:17.201 --> 09:19.451
just a big bushel of red flags.

09:19.541 --> 09:22.161
[DEALER] And for your
second bet, sir?

09:22.251 --> 09:23.421
[KIKUCHI] Hmm...

09:24.041 --> 09:26.921
I'll do the max again
and raise 30 chips.

09:28.591 --> 09:30.091
[DEALER] Mr. Akiyama?

09:30.171 --> 09:32.671
[KIKUCHI] I think we all know
where this is going.

09:32.761 --> 09:34.051
[inhales]

09:34.141 --> 09:36.391
Here, I'm gonna help you out
a little bit, 'kay?

09:36.471 --> 09:38.681
Why not?
My cards are such shit,

09:38.771 --> 09:41.021
there's no way
I can win this hand.

09:41.101 --> 09:44.651
So call. You were
never gonna fold anyway.

09:45.771 --> 09:46.861
I call.

09:46.941 --> 09:48.111
[SOLARIO] Astounding.

09:48.191 --> 09:50.651
The pot is now
a whopping 50 chips.

09:50.741 --> 09:52.321
But who will claim it?

09:52.401 --> 09:53.701
[DEALER] Players...

09:53.781 --> 09:54.911
Open!

09:57.241 --> 09:58.491
[SOLARIO] With four queens,

09:58.581 --> 10:01.581
Kikuchi of the Western Army
claims the pot.

10:01.661 --> 10:02.911
[both gasp]

10:03.001 --> 10:04.461
[Kikuchi chuckles]

10:04.541 --> 10:08.171
Like I'd ever allow myself
to end up with a bunk hand.

10:09.001 --> 10:10.421
Not that I was worried,

10:10.511 --> 10:12.721
since the joker was
the second card down.

10:12.801 --> 10:15.681
Of course, I always know
where the joker is,

10:15.761 --> 10:18.681
which is why I'm invincible
in this game.

10:18.761 --> 10:21.181
You did this,
you bleeding heart.

10:21.271 --> 10:22.891
You had to tell them
we were trying

10:22.981 --> 10:24.601
to keep chips away
from the dealer.

10:24.691 --> 10:26.191
And now they're armed
with the knowledge

10:26.271 --> 10:28.191
that Akiyama
can't possibly fold.

10:28.271 --> 10:30.021
But I was...

10:30.111 --> 10:32.491
[SOLARIO] We end this hand
with the Western Army

10:32.571 --> 10:33.441
fifty chips richer.

10:34.571 --> 10:36.701
Putting them 118 chips ahead.

10:36.781 --> 10:40.241
With only three hands left,
is it over for the Eastern Army?

10:40.331 --> 10:42.501
[AKIYAMA] I graciously
called your bet,

10:42.581 --> 10:44.911
knowing full well that you'd
walk away with the pot,

10:45.001 --> 10:46.501
and you mock me for it?

10:46.831 --> 10:48.501
All right then, man.

10:48.591 --> 10:51.131
Just know you brought this down
upon yourself.

10:52.761 --> 10:55.091
[DEALER] We'll now move on
to our eighth hand.

10:55.551 --> 10:56.801
[AKIYAMA] Hold on, please.

10:56.891 --> 10:58.471
You have been letting
the cards show.

10:58.551 --> 10:59.551
[DEALER] Ah!

10:59.931 --> 11:02.141
And furthermore,
Kikuchi's been exploiting that

11:02.221 --> 11:04.101
to memorize the card order
while you shuffle.

11:04.181 --> 11:05.521
I have not.

11:05.811 --> 11:08.021
You're only saying that because
I'm beating you so badly.

11:08.101 --> 11:09.861
[AKIYAMA] I'm saying it
'cause it's true.

11:09.941 --> 11:11.651
You've made it painfully clear

11:11.731 --> 11:13.571
that you know
the joker's location.

11:13.651 --> 11:15.491
-Wait, is he serious?
-[gasps]

11:15.571 --> 11:17.241
These games are fair,
aren't they?

11:17.321 --> 11:18.781
That's what you've told us.

11:18.871 --> 11:20.531
[DEALER]
We strive for that, yes.

11:20.621 --> 11:23.911
Doing only the riffle shuffle
should solve the issue.

11:24.001 --> 11:26.581
That way,
Kikuchi can't follow the cards

11:26.661 --> 11:28.921
since they'll all be face down
on the table.

11:29.581 --> 11:31.751
I'm sure you'd be
agreeable to that.

11:31.841 --> 11:34.131
Prove your innocence
and whatnot.

11:34.881 --> 11:36.131
Very well, then.

11:36.221 --> 11:38.551
If it'll make you feel better,
let's go for it.

11:38.641 --> 11:40.601
Great. Then you may continue.

11:40.681 --> 11:42.891
[Kikuchi scoffs] What an idiot.

11:42.971 --> 11:45.601
The dealer can do
whatever shuffle he wants.

11:45.681 --> 11:47.021
It won't stop my plan.

11:47.101 --> 11:50.361
In fact, the joke's on you
because the riffle shuffle

11:50.441 --> 11:52.521
is easier to follow
than a Hindu.

11:53.691 --> 11:56.491
This is the last bit of kindness
I'll give you.

11:56.571 --> 11:58.491
From here on,
the gloves are coming off.

11:59.151 --> 12:01.281
I'm going to destroy you.

12:01.371 --> 12:02.491
That right?

12:02.571 --> 12:04.491
Trying to get
under my skin, huh?

12:04.581 --> 12:06.911
Then do your worst
because no matter what you do,

12:07.001 --> 12:08.871
I'm still going to win!

12:09.501 --> 12:10.921
♪

12:11.581 --> 12:14.211
Looks like the joker
is the fourth card down.

12:14.291 --> 12:16.711
[DEALER]
Your first bet, if you would.

12:17.171 --> 12:19.631
[KIKUCHI] I need to make sure
he stays in the game.

12:19.721 --> 12:22.801
Which he'll more than likely do
if he thinks I have a bad hand.

12:22.891 --> 12:24.601
So I'll start off small.

12:24.681 --> 12:25.971
Five chips.

12:26.061 --> 12:28.731
Really? Just five?

12:28.811 --> 12:30.401
[DEALER] And for you, sir?

12:32.691 --> 12:35.521
The max sounds good.
I'll do 15 chips.

12:35.611 --> 12:37.321
[all gasp]

12:37.401 --> 12:38.691
[DEALER] Your response?

12:39.821 --> 12:41.071
I will call.

12:41.151 --> 12:42.911
I knew I could keep him
in the game,

12:42.991 --> 12:45.331
but I didn't expect him
to bet the max.

12:45.411 --> 12:48.081
[DEALER] Does anyone have cards
to discard?

12:48.161 --> 12:49.501
[KIKUCHI] Obviously,
he won't discard

12:49.581 --> 12:50.661
more than three.

12:51.041 --> 12:53.581
So I can sit back
and let the joker come to me.

12:54.091 --> 12:56.001
Yes, I'll do all five.

12:56.091 --> 12:57.961
[KIKUCHI] No way!

12:59.131 --> 13:01.841
Now that stupid,
sneaky jerk has the joker!

13:01.931 --> 13:04.641
[DEALER] And how many cards
for you, Mr. Kikuchi?

13:05.351 --> 13:06.931
[KIKUCHI] Just one, please.

13:09.351 --> 13:12.311
Hmm, this is actually
a really good hand.

13:13.271 --> 13:15.271
Akiyama's
still a problem, though.

13:15.361 --> 13:17.361
[DEALER] Your second bet,
Mr. Akiyama.

13:17.731 --> 13:20.241
[KIKUCHI] If he goes big,
then I'll have to fold.

13:20.781 --> 13:22.821
Think I'll just do 15 again.

13:22.901 --> 13:25.121
[KIKUCHI] Huh?
Wait, is that all?

13:25.201 --> 13:29.541
Maybe his hand's not so hot.
Wow, I really lucked out.

13:29.621 --> 13:31.871
-[DEALER] Mr. Kikuchi.
-[KIKUCHI] Hmm.

13:33.211 --> 13:34.501
I call.

13:34.581 --> 13:37.251
[DEALER] Very good. Open!

13:38.251 --> 13:39.841
[SOLARIO]
And with four of a kind,

13:39.921 --> 13:42.261
the East triumphs over the West.

13:42.591 --> 13:43.681
What?

13:44.341 --> 13:47.301
[SOLARIO] With that, Akiyama has
broken Kikuchi's winning streak.

13:47.391 --> 13:49.971
And brought the West's lead
down to 48 chips.

13:51.101 --> 13:53.141
That was incredible.

13:53.231 --> 13:54.271
[KIKUCHI] It's fine.

13:54.351 --> 13:56.151
I knew I'd lose
one or two hands.

13:56.231 --> 13:58.651
Actually,
it's better that I lost,

13:58.731 --> 14:00.901
because now I get to cut second.

14:00.991 --> 14:03.861
And that'll make it much easier
to ensure I get the joker.

14:03.951 --> 14:07.121
More than that,
now I'll be able to guarantee

14:07.201 --> 14:09.331
that the joker ends up
in my opening hand.

14:09.411 --> 14:12.911
Which means there is
no possible way for me to lose!

14:13.711 --> 14:16.381
[DEALER] We'll now begin
our penultimate hand.

14:16.461 --> 14:18.711
All right, it's time
to lock it in.

14:18.791 --> 14:21.261
[Kikuchi laughs]
Sure, whatever you say!

14:21.341 --> 14:25.391
It's too late, but I'll hang
with you for a bit this hand.

14:30.141 --> 14:31.641
[DEALER]
I'll now deal the cards.

14:31.721 --> 14:33.061
[AKIYAMA]
Sorry to be annoying.

14:33.601 --> 14:35.811
But I noticed Kikuchi got a peek
at the cards

14:35.901 --> 14:37.151
while you were shuffling.

14:37.231 --> 14:39.021
Could you please
shuffle them again?

14:39.111 --> 14:41.111
Can we just play the game?

14:41.191 --> 14:42.821
[DEALER] Do you object,
Mr. Kikuchi?

14:42.901 --> 14:43.861
[Kikuchi grunts]

14:44.281 --> 14:46.611
I didn't expect him
to harp on me like this,

14:46.701 --> 14:48.781
but if I object,
I'll look like a cheater,

14:48.871 --> 14:50.991
which will just make
more problems for me.

14:51.281 --> 14:52.411
Not at all.

14:54.081 --> 14:55.581
[DEALER] Is that satisfactory?

14:55.661 --> 14:57.581
Very. Thank you.

14:57.961 --> 15:00.211
[DEALER]
Wonderful. And the cut, sir?

15:00.751 --> 15:02.551
Let's say, five cards.

15:02.631 --> 15:03.801
Four cards, please.

15:03.881 --> 15:05.841
It's all coming together.

15:05.921 --> 15:08.301
That cut put the joker
right where I want it.

15:09.511 --> 15:12.351
Since he cut first,
Akiyama will be dealt in first,

15:12.431 --> 15:15.391
which puts the joker
squarely into my hand.

15:16.601 --> 15:19.941
And that gives me three aces!
Too good!

15:20.021 --> 15:22.321
[DEALER] Would you start us off,
Mr. Akiyama?

15:22.401 --> 15:23.481
[AKIYAMA] Hmm.

15:23.571 --> 15:24.991
I'm gonna check.

15:25.071 --> 15:26.701
[KIKUCHI] He's gonna what?!

15:26.781 --> 15:28.781
Oh, I know what you're doing.

15:28.871 --> 15:31.371
Making me go first
to feel out my hand.

15:31.451 --> 15:33.451
Well, then, feel this out.

15:33.541 --> 15:34.951
Eight chips.

15:35.041 --> 15:38.371
Just eight?
Figured you'd go bigger.

15:38.461 --> 15:39.461
All right.

15:40.081 --> 15:41.461
I'll call.

15:41.541 --> 15:43.631
[KIKUCHI] That's right, idiot!
Take the bait!

15:43.711 --> 15:46.131
[DEALER] Do you wish to discard,
Mr. Kikuchi?

15:46.511 --> 15:48.471
Yes. Two cards, please.

15:48.551 --> 15:50.261
[laughs]

15:50.341 --> 15:54.221
Full house! Aces full of jacks!
I'm unstoppable!

15:54.311 --> 15:55.891
[DEALER] Mr. Akiyama?

15:55.981 --> 15:57.231
[AKIYAMA] Hmm...

15:57.311 --> 15:59.401
Know what? I'll take five.

15:59.481 --> 16:02.061
[KIKUCHI] He's dumping
his whole hand?

16:02.151 --> 16:04.021
What is going on?

16:04.111 --> 16:06.151
Is he spiraling
that badly already?

16:06.241 --> 16:08.491
[DEALER] Mr. Kikuchi,
it's your turn to start us off.

16:08.571 --> 16:10.361
[KIKUCHI]
I'm in a prime position

16:10.451 --> 16:12.531
to finish him off.
But to do that,

16:12.621 --> 16:14.451
I need to make sure
he calls my bet.

16:14.531 --> 16:16.911
And to do that,
I have to convince him

16:17.001 --> 16:18.621
that my hand is utter trash.

16:18.711 --> 16:20.461
I'll just do eight again.

16:21.381 --> 16:23.001
That's interesting.

16:23.091 --> 16:24.751
[DEALER] And you, Mr. Akiyama?

16:24.841 --> 16:28.261
All right, I'll raise.
Let's do the 30-chip maximum.

16:28.341 --> 16:29.881
[Kikuchi screams]

16:29.971 --> 16:31.091
[AKIYAMA] Hm?

16:31.181 --> 16:33.051
[KIKUCHI]
This guy's a grade A moron!

16:33.141 --> 16:35.811
He's so convinced
my hand is terrible

16:35.891 --> 16:37.141
that he went all in.

16:37.481 --> 16:40.391
I don't think I've met
a bigger rube in my entire life!

16:40.481 --> 16:42.441
[DEALER] Your response,
Mr. Kikuchi?

16:42.521 --> 16:45.651
Hmm. I've got no choice.
Guess I have to call.

16:46.191 --> 16:48.901
Oh, this is gonna be so good.

16:49.571 --> 16:51.821
[DEALER] With that,
we move to finish this hand

16:51.911 --> 16:54.201
with an impressive 43 chips
on the table.

16:54.531 --> 16:55.781
Ready?

16:55.871 --> 16:57.291
Open!

16:57.661 --> 16:59.791
[KIKUCHI] Die, Akiyama!

17:03.381 --> 17:04.291
[Kikuchi gasps]

17:04.381 --> 17:05.881
[screaming]

17:05.961 --> 17:07.631
[SOLARIO] Akiyama takes the pot.

17:07.711 --> 17:08.761
Way to go!

17:09.261 --> 17:10.921
[SOLARIO] The Eastern Army
has done the improbable.

17:13.261 --> 17:17.601
However, only our final hand
will determine ultimate victory.

17:17.681 --> 17:19.521
-[Akiyama chuckles]
-[KIKUCHI] That was luck.

17:19.601 --> 17:22.601
Pure, stupid, dumb luck!
He can't do it again.

17:22.691 --> 17:24.521
There's no way
he'll draw four of a kind

17:24.611 --> 17:26.361
on a five-card draw this hand.

17:26.441 --> 17:29.611
And since I lost again,
I'll be cutting the deck second.

17:29.691 --> 17:31.571
Which means in the final hand,

17:31.651 --> 17:33.911
I'll get the joker
right out of the gate!

17:33.991 --> 17:37.621
Mark my words, Akiyama.
You will lose!

17:38.241 --> 17:39.581
[DEALER] Welcome, players,

17:39.661 --> 17:42.041
to the beginning
of our final hand.

17:42.121 --> 17:44.791
[KIKUCHI] Now, of course,
the question isn't if I can win.

17:44.881 --> 17:47.171
It's if he's gonna fold
and end the game,

17:47.251 --> 17:48.631
or ride it out.

17:48.711 --> 17:50.761
-[AKIYAMA] Hey, don't worry.
-Uh?

17:50.841 --> 17:52.921
I'll see this through
to the end.

17:53.011 --> 17:55.011
-[gasps]
-[AKIYAMA] You're surprised?

17:55.091 --> 17:57.051
I could see the concern
on your face.

17:57.141 --> 17:58.971
You're scared that
since I'm winning,

17:59.061 --> 18:01.731
I'll just fold
and end the match. Am I right?

18:01.811 --> 18:05.311
I could, as we could've
in the Spearhead match.

18:05.401 --> 18:08.151
But we didn't cut and run then,
and I won't now.

18:08.231 --> 18:10.901
Because the important thing
isn't eking out a win

18:10.981 --> 18:12.071
however you can.

18:12.151 --> 18:13.451
It's securing enough cash

18:13.531 --> 18:16.161
to survive a loss
in the Liar Game overall.

18:16.781 --> 18:18.871
And right now,
momentum's on my side.

18:18.951 --> 18:20.161
I expect to win,

18:20.241 --> 18:22.701
so I'm setting myself up
for a big windfall.

18:23.411 --> 18:26.251
[KIKUCHI] Oh, you've really
got yourself convinced, huh?

18:26.331 --> 18:29.551
[muffled giggling]
More power to you, you moron.

18:29.631 --> 18:31.171
♪

18:33.381 --> 18:35.801
The joker is the ninth card
from the top.

18:35.891 --> 18:36.891
-[AKIYAMA] Sorry.
-Uh?

18:36.971 --> 18:38.601
One last thing.

18:38.681 --> 18:39.971
This is the final hand,

18:40.061 --> 18:41.771
so let's leave no room
for doubt.

18:41.851 --> 18:43.981
Please shuffle the deck
three more times.

18:44.061 --> 18:47.361
Are you se--
No, fine. Let's do it.

18:47.441 --> 18:48.811
If that's what
it's going to take

18:48.901 --> 18:49.861
to ease your mind.

18:49.941 --> 18:51.111
It is.

18:52.031 --> 18:53.821
All right,
shuffle them again.

18:53.901 --> 18:55.361
[DEALER] Very well, then.

19:00.411 --> 19:01.831
[cards shuffling]

19:02.701 --> 19:05.251
[DEALER] Now to cut the deck...
Mr. Akiyama?

19:05.751 --> 19:07.541
Let's see. Eight cards.

19:07.631 --> 19:09.291
Seven for me, please.

19:09.381 --> 19:13.051
And that will put the joker
sixth from the top of the deck.

19:13.551 --> 19:16.591
Which will ensure it ends up
in my opening hand!

19:17.641 --> 19:20.641
Aces full of kings!
This is perfect!

19:20.721 --> 19:22.391
I don't have
to discard anything!

19:22.471 --> 19:23.681
Question now is...

19:24.221 --> 19:27.401
Will Akiyama make good
on his word to stay in the game?

19:27.481 --> 19:29.481
[DEALER]
It's your bet, Mr. Akiyama.

19:29.561 --> 19:30.901
[AKIYAMA] Hmm.

19:31.481 --> 19:32.731
I'll do 15 chips.

19:32.821 --> 19:34.071
Fifteen?

19:34.481 --> 19:38.321
I told you. I believe I can win,
so I won't be holding back.

19:38.411 --> 19:40.411
[KIKUCHI] That's more like it!

19:40.491 --> 19:43.621
His gambler brain is making him
even stupider than before!

19:43.701 --> 19:45.621
He's gonna lose so much money!

19:45.701 --> 19:47.161
[DEALER] Mr. Kikuchi?

19:47.251 --> 19:50.381
Right, well.
I am pretty far behind.

19:50.461 --> 19:52.461
I guess I'll have to call then.

19:52.551 --> 19:54.671
[DEALER] Very good.
You may now discard.

19:54.751 --> 19:56.881
-Mr. Akiyama?
-Yeah...

19:58.011 --> 19:59.931
I'm gonna discard my whole hand.

20:00.011 --> 20:02.051
[yelps]

20:02.471 --> 20:03.471
You good?

20:03.561 --> 20:05.971
[KIKUCHI] What?
Oh, yes. So good.

20:06.431 --> 20:09.151
This guy went all in
on a garbage hand.

20:09.231 --> 20:11.151
No, that can't be it.

20:11.231 --> 20:13.321
Maybe he thinks
the joker is still in the deck,

20:13.401 --> 20:15.691
and he's desperately trying
to get it.

20:15.781 --> 20:16.781
Oh, well.

20:17.241 --> 20:19.531
Too bad I already made sure
it'd find its way to me!

20:19.611 --> 20:21.411
Still, makes things tricky.

20:21.491 --> 20:23.081
There are only two cards left,

20:23.161 --> 20:25.241
and you only draw one
if you have the joker.

20:25.331 --> 20:26.411
But if I draw two,

20:26.491 --> 20:27.871
we'll have gone through
the whole deck,

20:27.951 --> 20:29.411
and he'll know I have it.

20:30.081 --> 20:31.711
Seems like no matter what I do,

20:31.791 --> 20:33.921
I'll be showing my hand,
as it were.

20:34.001 --> 20:36.211
And he'll fold immediately
after that.

20:36.301 --> 20:39.301
Wait, what if I do nothing?
It's so simple.

20:39.381 --> 20:41.141
I keep my hand
and then just pretend

20:41.221 --> 20:42.221
like the joker is still

20:42.511 --> 20:44.351
one of the remaining cards
in the deck.

20:45.011 --> 20:46.851
Your whole hand again, huh?

20:46.931 --> 20:48.221
Well, then...

20:48.311 --> 20:50.771
These lousy cards
might stand a chance after all.

20:50.851 --> 20:51.811
[AKIYAMA] Hm?

20:51.901 --> 20:54.571
Here goes.
I am keeping my hand.

20:54.651 --> 20:56.071
Besides, it's not like

20:56.151 --> 20:58.361
the odds of my improving
on it now are any good.

20:58.441 --> 20:59.401
Guess I could try,

21:00.071 --> 21:02.071
but that would just give you
another reason to fold, so...

21:02.161 --> 21:03.661
I won't!

21:03.741 --> 21:05.831
Instead, I'll risk it all
on this garbage!

21:06.621 --> 21:08.501
I can't tell if he bought it.

21:09.121 --> 21:11.791
Oh, no!
Did I lay it on too thick?

21:11.871 --> 21:14.131
[DEALER] Let's move on
to the second round of betting.

21:14.211 --> 21:15.751
Mr. Akiyama, if you would.

21:15.841 --> 21:18.961
[KIKUCHI] Stay in!
Stay in, stay in, stay in!

21:19.051 --> 21:20.221
Huh.

21:20.841 --> 21:22.051
I know.

21:22.641 --> 21:25.011
The max, 30 chips.

21:25.101 --> 21:26.511
[Kikuchi squeals]

21:27.101 --> 21:29.141
Sorry, could you repeat that?

21:29.221 --> 21:31.391
Hmm? Yeah, I said 30.

21:31.481 --> 21:33.811
Couldn't see a reason
to play it safe.

21:34.231 --> 21:35.561
Oh, I see.

21:35.651 --> 21:37.361
I won.

21:37.441 --> 21:40.321
By the power
of my acting, I won.

21:40.401 --> 21:42.571
[DEALER] And for your bet,
Mr. Kikuchi?

21:43.201 --> 21:45.571
I'll call. It's only fair.

21:45.661 --> 21:48.241
[DEALER] Very good.
The hand is now complete.

21:48.331 --> 21:49.791
[Kikuchi chuckles]

21:49.871 --> 21:50.871
[laughs]

21:51.411 --> 21:55.331
Yes! And that's the game!
You just got played, Akiyama!

21:55.421 --> 21:56.501
I what?

21:56.791 --> 21:58.921
You got played!
And now that the hand's over,

21:59.001 --> 22:01.841
I'm gonna tell you how!
You see, you were right.

22:01.921 --> 22:02.921
I knew!

22:03.381 --> 22:05.511
I've known where the joker was
for most of the game!

22:05.591 --> 22:07.221
I've won.

22:07.301 --> 22:09.471
And you never saw it coming!

22:09.561 --> 22:12.931
[laughing]

22:15.101 --> 22:17.481
[♪ closing theme song playing]
